  "how_written": "On 2026-11-21, by an agent that had read the README's paragraph on the guardrail and issue #116, and had read neither guard.py nor its tests. 'blind' is the verdict written then; 'expected' is the verdict after the guardrail ran on the draft, and 'decision' says why wherever the two differ or the guardrail is known to be wrong. No command was added after the code was read. The author of the corpus is not the author of the guardrail, but is a model of the same family: the corpus says what this draft found, not how often the guardrail is wrong on a team's real commands.",
  "verdicts": {
    "deliver": "creates or pushes a tag, creates a release, starts a workflow, publishes or deploys: the guardrail refuses it",
    "pass-through": "delivers, or may deliver, and the guardrail lets it through: a known limit, listed in README.md. 'refused_when_quoted' says whether the guardrail refuses it once docs/agents/delivery.md quotes the command",
    "false-refusal": "ordinary work the guardrail refuses today: a known defect, listed in README.md",
    "benign": "ordinary work, often one that looks like a delivery: the guardrail lets it through"
  },
